      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Perhaps we should just get an FBT toggle in the quick menu, just like the index gesture type toggle. Toggling it off and on would initiate calibration again.\n\nSadly and ironically, FBT users are second class citizens in this game. FBT has been \"barely functional\" from day one, requiring all sorts of hacky armature mangling to be functional. Even the default avatars have bent legs, and the chest clips into the viewpoint when sitting.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-03T17:16:40.990Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Every time I launch the game and first enter my home world the blue loading avatar gets stuck in a T pose and I can see my tracker balls and controllers, similar to when I'm calibrating into my avatar. I'm also unable to move. However, I retain the ability to move and make the loading avatar unstuck from the T pose by calibrating.\n\nHowever, this messes up the calibration for the avatar that I was supposed to load into... to comedic effect: https://youtu.be/3DFIs7dJ3BM\n\nHere's an output log for the devs: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Y7BbbvyK3AXFZs2e9ox4dQfU74qWFxxb/view?usp=sharing\n\nRepro steps:\n-Launch VRChat with 6 point IK full body tracking\n-Upon loading into the world and having the blue loading avatar T-pose for calibration, calibrate\n-The avatar you are loading into will take the calibration from the blue loading avatar and mess up the model",
  "error": null,
